{"version":"6.9","hitCount":1,"request":{"queryString":"TITLE:\"Cardiovascular toxicity and titin cross-reactivity\" AND SRC:MED","resultType":"core","cursorMark":"*","pageSize":6,"sort":"","synonym":false},"resultList":{"result":[{"id":"23770775","source":"MED","pmid":"23770775","pmcid":"PMC3743463","fullTextIdList":{"fullTextId":["PMC3743463"]},"doi":"10.1182/blood-2013-03-490565","title":"Cardiovascular toxicity and titin cross-reactivity of affinity-enhanced T cells in myeloma and melanoma.","authorString":"Linette GP, Stadtmauer EA, Maus MV, Rapoport AP, Levine BL, Emery L, Litzky L, Bagg A, Carreno BM, Cimino PJ, Binder-Scholl GK, Smethurst DP, Gerry AB, Pumphrey NJ, Bennett AD, Brewer JE, Dukes J, Harper J, Tayton-Martin HK, Jakobsen BK, Hassan NJ, Kalos M, June CH.","authorList":{"author":[{"fullName":"Linette GP","lastName":"Linette","firstName":"Gerald P","initials":"GP","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Siteman Cancer Center and Departments of Medicine and Pathology and Immunology, Washington University School of Medicine, St. Louis, MO, USA."}]}},{"fullName":"Stadtmauer EA","lastName":"Stadtmauer","firstName":"Edward A","initials":"EA"},{"fullName":"Maus MV","lastName":"Maus","firstName":"Marcela V","initials":"MV"},{"fullName":"Rapoport AP","lastName":"Rapoport","firstName":"Aaron P","initials":"AP"},{"fullName":"Levine BL","lastName":"Levine","firstName":"Bruce L","initials":"BL"},{"fullName":"Emery L","lastName":"Emery","firstName":"Lyndsey","initials":"L"},{"fullName":"Litzky L","lastName":"Litzky","firstName":"Leslie","initials":"L"},{"fullName":"Bagg A","lastName":"Bagg","firstName":"Adam","initials":"A"},{"fullName":"Carreno BM","lastName":"Carreno","firstName":"Beatriz M","initials":"BM"},{"fullName":"Cimino PJ","lastName":"Cimino","firstName":"Patrick J","initials":"PJ","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0003-0441-4502"}},{"fullName":"Binder-Scholl GK","lastName":"Binder-Scholl","firstName":"Gwendolyn K","initials":"GK"},{"fullName":"Smethurst DP","lastName":"Smethurst","firstName":"Dominic P","initials":"DP"},{"fullName":"Gerry AB","lastName":"Gerry","firstName":"Andrew B","initials":"AB"},{"fullName":"Pumphrey NJ","lastName":"Pumphrey","firstName":"Nick J","initials":"NJ"},{"fullName":"Bennett AD","lastName":"Bennett","firstName":"Alan D","initials":"AD"},{"fullName":"Brewer JE","lastName":"Brewer","firstName":"Joanna E","initials":"JE"},{"fullName":"Dukes J","lastName":"Dukes","firstName":"Joseph","initials":"J"},{"fullName":"Harper J","lastName":"Harper","firstName":"Jane","initials":"J"},{"fullName":"Tayton-Martin HK","lastName":"Tayton-Martin","firstName":"Helen K","initials":"HK"},{"fullName":"Jakobsen BK","lastName":"Jakobsen","firstName":"Bent K","initials":"BK"},{"fullName":"Hassan NJ","lastName":"Hassan","firstName":"Namir J","initials":"NJ"},{"fullName":"Kalos M","lastName":"Kalos","firstName":"Michael","initials":"M","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0009-0009-5745-2634"}},{"fullName":"June CH","lastName":"June","firstName":"Carl H","initials":"CH"}]},"authorIdList":{"authorId":[{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0003-0441-4502"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0009-0009-5745-2634"}]},"dataLinksTagsList":{"dataLinkstag":["supporting_data","protocols","wikipedia"]},"journalInfo":{"issue":"6","volume":"122","journalIssueId":2065094,"dateOfPublication":"2013 Aug","monthOfPublication":8,"yearOfPublication":2013,"journal":{"medlineAbbreviation":"Blood","title":"Blood","essn":"1528-0020","issn":"0006-4971","isoabbreviation":"Blood","nlmid":"7603509"},"printPublicationDate":"2013-08-01"},"pubYear":"2013","pageInfo":"863-871","abstractText":"An obstacle to cancer immunotherapy has been that the affinity of T-cell receptors (TCRs) for antigens expressed in tumors is generally low. We initiated clinical testing of engineered T cells expressing an affinity-enhanced TCR against HLA-A*01-restricted MAGE-A3. Open-label protocols to test the TCRs for patients with myeloma and melanoma were initiated. The first two treated patients developed cardiogenic shock and died within a few days of T-cell infusion, events not predicted by preclinical studies of the high-affinity TCRs. Gross findings at autopsy revealed severe myocardial damage, and histopathological analysis revealed T-cell infiltration. No MAGE-A3 expression was detected in heart autopsy tissues. Robust proliferation of the engineered T cells in vivo was documented in both patients. A beating cardiomyocyte culture generated from induced pluripotent stem cells triggered T-cell killing, which was due to recognition of an unrelated peptide derived from the striated muscle-specific protein titin. These patients demonstrate that TCR-engineered T cells can have serious and not readily predictable off-target and organ-specific toxicities and highlight the need for improved methods to define the specificity of engineered TCRs.","affiliation":"Siteman Cancer Center and Departments of Medicine and Pathology and Immunology, Washington University School of Medicine, St. Louis, MO, USA.","publicationStatus":"ppublish","language":"eng","pubModel":"Print-Electronic","pubTypeList":{"pubType":["research-article","Journal Article"]},"grantsList":{"grant":[{"agency":"NCI NIH HHS","acronym":"CA","grantId":"P30 CA016520","orderIn":0},{"agency":"NCI NIH HHS","acronym":"CA","grantId":"K08 CA166039","orderIn":0},{"agency":"NCI NIH HHS","acronym":"CA","grantId":"R01 CA166961","orderIn":0}]},"meshHeadingList":{"meshHeading":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Myocardium","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"IM","qualifierName":"immunology"},{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","abbreviation":"PA","qualifierName":"pathology"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"T-Lymphocytes","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","abbreviation":"CY","qualifierName":"cytology"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Humans"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Multipl